      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "BLOOM Charity distinguishes itself through a unique focus on 'therapeutic play' as a core component of humanitarian aid. By constructing <cite id=\"11\">11 PlayGardens</cite> to date, they address the long-term psychological needs of orphans that are often overlooked in traditional relief models. Their financial health is robust, evidenced by <cite id=\"12\">21.3 months of operating reserves</cite> and an <cite id=\"13\">overall score of 89.5/100 from Charity Navigator</cite>. This combination of specialized service delivery and fiscal discipline makes them a standout in the small-to-midsize humanitarian sector."
      ],
      "summary": "BLOOM Charity is a specialized humanitarian organization dedicated to the mental health and physical well-being of vulnerable children, particularly orphans in Morocco and Gaza. Founded in <cite id=\"1\">2015</cite>, the organization has rapidly expanded its footprint from building therapeutic <cite id=\"2\">PlayGardens in Morocco</cite> to providing critical emergency relief in conflict zones. In FY2024, the charity demonstrated significant growth, reporting <cite id=\"3\">total revenue of $551,810</cite>, a substantial increase from its <cite id=\"4\">FY2022 revenue of $107,186</cite>. This early-stage growth reflects a high demand for its niche services, which combine long-term developmental support with immediate crisis response. The organization maintains an exceptional <cite id=\"5\">program expense ratio of 98.7%</cite> based on its latest filings, ensuring that donor contributions are directed almost entirely to frontline services. During the 2024 period, BLOOM's impact was particularly visible in Gaza, where they provided <cite id=\"6\">700,000 meals</cite> and continued their mission of creating safe spaces for children. Their model is highly efficient, with <cite id=\"7\">fundraising costs of just <$0.01 per $1 raised</cite>, allowing for a lean operation that maximizes direct aid. As a <cite id=\"8\">zakat-eligible organization</cite>, BLOOM provides a verified pathway for Muslim donors to support the <cite id=\"9\">fuqara (poor) and masakin (needy)</cite> through specialized childhood enrichment and trauma-informed care.",
